P["springfield-mo-bulk-trash-pickup.html"]=("Springfield MO bulk trash pickup: who picks it up and what it costs (2026)","Does Springfield, MO pick up bulk trash? How bulky item pickup works with private haulers, plus drop-off sites and fees from official city pages.",f"""<h1>Bulk trash pickup in Springfield, MO</h1>
<p class="lede">Short answer: the City of Springfield does not run its own trash trucks. Your private trash hauler handles pickup, so they are the ones to ask about big items. If they can't help, you can drop items off yourself.</p>{glance("City of Springfield, Republic Services")}
<section class="step step-city"><h2>Step 1: Call your own trash hauler</h2><ul><li>Trash in Springfield is picked up by <strong>more than 10 private, licensed hauling companies</strong>. You pick your own.{S(C,"City of Springfield")}</li><li>Ask your hauler: Do you pick up couches, mattresses, or appliances? What does it cost? How should I set it out?</li><li>Not sure who your hauler is? Check your trash bill.</li></ul></section>
<section class="step step-city"><h2>Step 2: How to set items out (Republic Services example)</h2><ul><li>Republic Services offers bulk pickup in some areas. It asks you to <strong>wrap mattresses in plastic</strong>, leave sofas and chairs <strong>in one piece</strong>, and take the doors off fridges and washers.{S(REP,"Republic Services")}</li><li>Other haulers may have different rules. Ask yours.</li></ul></section>
<section class="step step-city"><h2>Step 3: Or drop it off yourself</h2><ul><li><strong>Mattresses and box springs: $20 per piece</strong> at three city sites. They must be clean, dry, and free of bugs.{S(M,"Mattress Recycling page")}{MATT}</li><li><strong>Couches and other junk:</strong> Noble Hill Sanitary Landfill charges <strong>$43.85 per ton, $20 minimum</strong> per vehicle. Cash, check, and cards. Phone 417-742-3536.{S(L,"Landfill page")}</li><li>Recycling questions: city Recycling Hotline 417-864-1904.{S(R,"Recycling Centers page")}</li></ul></section>
<section class="step donate"><h2>Still good? Give it away</h2><p>Offer clean items free to neighbors, or call a thrift store or church first. Many charities do not take used mattresses.</p></section>{END}""")
P["mattress-recycling-fee-springfield-mo.html"]=("Mattress recycling fee in Springfield, MO: $20 per piece (2026)","Springfield, MO charges $20 per mattress or box spring to recycle it. Drop-off sites, hours, and what they won't take, from the official city page.",f"""<h1>Mattress recycling fee in Springfield, MO</h1>
<p class="lede">The City of Springfield charges <strong>$20 per piece</strong> to recycle a mattress or box spring, any size. A mattress plus a box spring is $40.{S(M,"Mattress Recycling page")}</p>{glance("City of Springfield")}
<section class="step step-city"><h2>Where to take it</h2>{MATT}<p>Source:{S(M,"City of Springfield Mattress Recycling")}</p></section>
<section class="step step-city"><h2>What they will and won't take</h2><ul><li>Taken: mattresses and box springs.</li><li>Not taken: <strong>wet</strong>, <strong>bug-infested</strong>, or <strong>heavily soiled</strong> items.</li><li>Paying: Franklin Avenue and Lone Pine take only <strong>cash or check</strong>. The landfill also takes cards.{S(R,"Recycling Centers page")}</li></ul></section>
<section class="step step-city"><h2>Where does it go?</h2><p>The program runs through a contract with Victory Mission, a local nonprofit. Mattresses are taken apart, and the parts become raw materials for things like building materials and wood chip mulch. The city says more than 12,000 mattresses have been collected since 2018.{S(M,"City of Springfield")}</p></section>
<section class="step donate"><h2>Tips</h2><ul><li>Keep it dry. Cover it if it rides in an open truck bed.</li><li>Live in Ozark or nearby? These are City of Springfield sites. Call the Recycling Hotline (417-864-1904) to ask if you can use them.</li></ul></section>{END}""")
P["where-to-dump-a-couch-springfield-mo.html"]=("Where to dump a couch in Springfield, MO (legal options and fees, 2026)","The legal ways to get rid of a couch in Springfield, MO: give it away, hauler pickup, or Noble Hill Landfill at $43.85 per ton with a $20 minimum.",f"""<h1>Where to dump a couch in Springfield, MO</h1>
<p class="lede">The main public place to take an old couch is the <strong>Noble Hill Sanitary Landfill</strong> near Willard. Before you haul it, see if someone can still use it.</p>{glance("City of Springfield, Republic Services")}
<section class="step donate"><h2>Option 1: Give it away</h2><p>If it is clean and in good shape, offer it free to neighbors (Buy Nothing groups, Nextdoor, Facebook Marketplace). Or call a thrift store or church and ask if they take couches and if they pick up.</p></section>
<section class="step step-city"><h2>Option 2: Take it to the landfill</h2><ul><li>Noble Hill Sanitary Landfill, 3545 W. Farm Road 34, Willard. Phone 417-742-3536.{S(L,"Landfill page")}</li><li>Fee: <strong>$43.85 per ton, with a $20 minimum</strong> per vehicle. One couch usually weighs far less than a ton, so expect to pay the minimum, but the scale decides.{S(L,"Landfill page")}</li><li>Pay with cash, check, or a card.</li><li>Call ahead to check hours before you go.</li></ul></section>
<section class="step step-city"><h2>Option 3: Ask your hauler for bulk pickup</h2><p>Springfield's trash is handled by more than 10 private haulers.{S(C,"City of Springfield")} Ask yours if they pick up furniture and what it costs. Republic Services asks that sofas be left in one piece.{S(REP,"Republic Services")}</p></section>
<section class="step step-other"><h2>Option 4: Hire a junk removal company</h2><p>Get a written price first. Never pay someone who might dump it illegally. See our <a href="junk-removal-springfield-ozark-mo.html">Springfield and Ozark junk removal guide</a> for company links. (Those are plain links, not affiliate links.)</p></section>
<p class="check">Do not leave a couch on the roadside or in an empty lot. That is illegal dumping.</p>{END}""")
